; Diagnostic WHO 1001, 1004, 1005, 1013 and 1018: the DIMENSION request numbers a gateway
; forwards or answers (*#1001*74*DIM##, *#1004*31*DIM##, *#1005*31*DIM##, *#1013*0*DIM##,
; *#1018*31*DIM##).
; Boundary probe of 2026-11-16 and 2026-11-17 on the 13 emulated gateways: the same values for
; every WHO, DIMENSION 0..30, 40, 50, 51, 54, 60, 100, 113, 255, 256, 1200. DIMENSION 0 of WHO
; 1013 (*#1013*0*0##) is left out on purpose: in 1 of 10 runs the answer of the F453AV carried
; one frame more (*#1013**7*...##), so the row is not reproducible.
;
; Result (stock settings, two identical runs per target, 13 targets): per group below, the
; gateways that forward the frame to the bus or answer it on the event session, and the
; gateways whose daemon crashes. Gateways not named drop the frame.

